--TEST--
A `yield` written where a value is consumed is `E0448`, the same code its three other missing spellings take — `rule:iteration/one-way-only` gives a generator no `send()`, so there is nothing for a resumed `yield` to hand back
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Counter {
    // `rule:iteration/one-way-only` gives a generator no `send()`, so a resumed `yield`
    // has nothing to hand back — the statement form is the whole of what
    // the construct is, and every other position is refused.
    public static function upTo(int $n): Iterator<int> {
        yield 1;
        mixed $answer = yield 2;
        echo $answer as string;
    }

    // The same refusal wherever the value is consumed. A condition is the
    // one position that accepts any type at all (`rule:expressions/truthy-positions`), so nothing
    // else is reported on this line and the `yield` is the whole of it.
    public static function tested(): Iterator<int> {
        yield 1;
        if (yield 2) {
            echo "x";
        }
    }
}

foreach (Counter::upTo(3) as int $v) {
    echo $v;
}
